/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 770 Tm (3. Retrieve a shipment) Tj
/F3 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 747 Tm (GET /v1/shipments/{shipment_id}) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 731 Tm (Returns one shipment with its status, parcels, carrier, service, cost and the timestamps of its) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 715 Tm (booking and last update. A shipment that was never booked returns 404.) Tj
/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 683 Tm (4. Track a parcel) Tj
/F3 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 660 Tm (GET /v1/tracking/{tracking_number}) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 644 Tm (Public tracking for a tracking number issued by any carrier. No API key is needed. The response) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 628 Tm (carries the current status \(one of pre_transit, in_transit, out_for_delivery, delivered or) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 612 Tm (exception\), an estimated_delivery date, and an events array. Each event has a timestamp, a city,) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 596 Tm (a country code and a description written for the recipient.) Tj
/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 564 Tm (Webhooks) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 541 Tm (Register an HTTPS endpoint in the dashboard to receive tracking.updated events. Each delivery is) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 525 Tm (signed with an HMAC-SHA256 digest of the body in the X-Lumen-Signature header.) Tj
/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 493 Tm (Rate limits) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 470 Tm (Each key may make 60 requests per minute. Above that the API answers 429 with Retry-After.) Tj
